course: dictionary
lesson: 1854
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To know which meaning is right, look at the context: the words and sentences around the word. «Cod» is a good example, because it can name a fish, mean fake, or stand for a way of paying.
explain: «Fish fingers are usually white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock, cut into blocks and breadcrumbed.» Cod is a fish here, because the words around it are fish names and fish fingers are made from fish. Always ask: what meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Now look at «a cod accent». Cod comes before another word and means fake or pretend, not real. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «a fake accent» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Cod is a large sea fish with white flesh, and it is eaten a lot as food, especially in fish and chips.
fact: «Cod» before a word means fake or pretend, not real, as in «a cod accent» or «cod science». This is informal, mostly used in the UK.
fact: COD stands for cash on delivery: you pay when goods are delivered, in some countries.
fact: Cod liver oil is a vitamin supplement, and «a spoon of cod-liver oil really helped» children with rickets.
fact: Around Newfoundland in Canada, so many cod were caught that the fishing was closed in 1992, and the cod have still not fully come back.
exercise: «Fish fingers are usually white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock.» What is cod in this sentence? | A fake, pretend thing | *A large sea fish | A way of paying when goods arrive | A type of bread
exercise: Max says, «That is a cod accent, it is not real.» What does cod mean here? | A large sea fish | *Fake or pretend | Very loud | Cash on delivery
exercise: «Cod and chips, please.» What does cod mean in this order at the chip shop? | A kind of bread roll | Fake, pretend food | *A fish, served with chips | Cash on delivery
test: «The parcel arrived, and we paid COD.» What does COD stand for? | Cold on doorstep | Customer order date | Cod on dinner | *Cash on delivery
test: «The Victorian cooks served whiting, a silvery fish of the cod family.» What does the cod family tell you? | Whiting is cooked in a family kitchen | *Whiting is related to cod, as another fish | Cod is a kind of family name | Whiting is a fake fish
exam: Ella reads «a cod review» and thinks it is a review about fish. Which is the best way to check her idea? | Look up cod in a fish book only | Guess, because cod always means fish | Skip the word and never think about it again | *Swap in fake or pretend and see if the sentence makes sense
